### Page content summary

- **Purpose:** Subjective “felt rhythm” overlay on top of `DET.VISUAL.RHYTHM` and `DET.LAYOUT.GRID_CONSISTENCY`—catches accidental grouping when numeric checks pass.
- **Passing signals:** Repeated section motif (`forge-section py-5`, `section-label text-cyan` → heading → grid), stable gutters (`g-3 g-lg-4`), uniform `forge-card` shells, stable container width.
- **Failing signals:** Accidental pile-up (`py-2` → `py-5` → `py-3`), grid drift (`col-md-4` + `col-md-6` + `col-md-2`), motif breaks, in-row card inconsistency, width whiplash.
- **Before example:** Failing HTML with cramped hero (`py-2 g-1`), mismatched outcome row (`forge-card` + `glass` + odd spans), broken “How it works” band.
- **After example:** Passing HTML with `landing-hero fs-landing-hero-band`, aligned three-up `forge-card card-amber breathe-link`, consistent `forge-section py-5` bands, `fs-marketing-stat-band` stat row.
- **Evidence and remediation:** Screenshot capture checklist + 6-step remediation with `DET.*` promotion guidance.
- **Related rules:** `DET.VISUAL.RHYTHM`, `DET.LAYOUT.GRID_CONSISTENCY`, `DET.SECTION.HEADING`, `AI.VISUAL.HIERARCHY_CONFIDENCE`, `AI.PREMIUM.ENTERPRISE_FEEL`, `AI.CONTEXT.BURDEN_SUBJECTIVE`.

### KS class verification

Before/after examples use real Kitchen Sink classes from `components/`, `css/`, and `marketing_sections.py`: `landing-hero`, `fs-landing-hero-band`, `forge-section`, `landing-hero-wide`, `landing-hero-grid-wrap`, `landing-hero-kicker`, `product-landing-title`, `forge-support`, `landing-hero-tagline`, `landing-hero-actions`, `btn-forge`, `btn-cyan-outline`, `section-label`, `forge-card`, `card-amber`, `card-label`, `breathe-link`, `breathe-static`, `fs-landing-section`, `fs-marketing-stat-band`, `glass`, plus hash/`data-ks-*` attributes.

No Mermaid, no Fleet-specific profiles, no check modules or registry edits.
